    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d417-a1">

                <pb facs="0745" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg675"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 683.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul Viosca to Mr.
                            Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">La Paz,
                                Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-08-17"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 17,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It has been reported from Mazatlan that in
                    the appeal of the Adriana case pending before the United Mexican States circuit
                    court at Culiacan, decision has been rendered by the said court fully confirming
                    the sentence of the district court here.</p>
                <p>The schooner Adriana will be sold by the authorities here at public auction in a
                    few days.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAS. VIOSCA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
